willow-stability-timelike demo — NOTICE

This directory (apps/willow-stability-timelike/) is a CPU-only stim toy of the
surface-code stability experiment. It is not a reproduction of the Willow
processor and it does not include Google's device data or circuit compiler.

Papers (attribution):
  Craig Gidney, "Stability Experiments: The Overlooked Dual of Memory
  Experiments", Quantum 6, 786 (2022), https://doi.org/10.22331/q-2022-08-24-786
  arXiv:2204.13834

  Google Quantum AI and Collaborators, "Resolving and Suppressing Temporally
  Correlated Noise in Quantum Error Correction", arXiv:2611.21578
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.21578
  Found via a bookmarked X post by @AEickbusch (the post was not fetched;
  the bookmark text was supplied with the task and checked against the paper):
  https://x.com/AEickbusch/status/2122798788431716360

Hardware numbers quoted from the paper (mu_T = 1.47 ± 0.25, walking floor
≤ 3.20×10^{-8} at 60 cycles, adaptive 38% / 34%) are marked QUOTED. They are
not outputs of this simulation. The bookmark's "four orders of magnitude
versus the literature" and the paper's "two orders of magnitude below the
standard construction" are different comparisons and are both recorded.

